# What no image build may send to the builder (#204). Owner: integrator.
#
# Every Dockerfile here builds from the repository root (src/Gateway/Dockerfile,
# fixtures/MockApi/Dockerfile, tools/bench/floor/Dockerfile), so without this file a workstation's
# build sent its whole working tree: the local certificate authority's private key, the scratch
# directory, Terraform's git-ignored variables, and its own bin/ and obj/, which `COPY src/ src/`
# laid over the image's linux-arm64 restore so that `dotnet publish --no-restore` failed with
# NETSDK1047 (#58, sitting C, stage C1). A clean CI checkout has none of these, which is why only a
# workstation showed it.
#
# A denylist that follows .gitignore, plus what git keeps out of the tree by other means. When
# .gitignore gains a secret, this file gains it too; tools/image_build_tests.py names one path for
# each thing below and holds this file to Docker's matching rules over them, and over every tracked
# file a Dockerfile copies.
#
# Docker matches each line with Go's filepath.Match from the context's root, so a bare `*.pem`
# matches only at the root and the patterns meant for any depth begin `**/`; a line also matches
# everything below a directory it names.
# https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#dockerignore-files

# git's own directory, and the .git file a linked worktree has instead.
.git

# Host build output. The image restores and publishes for its own architecture.
**/bin
**/obj
**/artifacts
**/TestResults
**/*.trx

# The local certificate authority and its keys (tools/scripts/certs.sh). Never send a private key.
.certs
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.srl

# Terraform's working directories, state, variables, backends and plans: they carry the account id,
# role ARNs, generated passwords and client secrets (.gitignore says which carries what).
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json
**/backend.hcl
**/*.tfplan
**/*.tfplan.json

# The infrastructure outputs document the deployment scripts write: the account id and both apps'
# client ids (contracts/infra-outputs.schema.json).
infra/envs/poc/outputs.json

# Local settings and secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local.env
**/*.local.json

# Agent and session scratch: the tracker archive, overnight logs, worktrees.
.scratch
.claude

# Editors and the OS.
**/.vs
**/.idea
**/*.user
**/.DS_Store
